{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1398569-first-mage-chronicle-not-sure-about-power-level","id":1398569,"title":"First mage chronicle, not sure about power level","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-24T02:52:38-07:00","id":1398569,"title":"First mage chronicle, not sure about power level","content":"Hi everybody!<br /> I'm new to storytelling mage 2e, just knew the rules of 1st edition. I come from a long V.TR chronicle though. I've got a small cabal of 1 acanthus, 1 obrimos and 1 mastigos. They all started with 5XP, to give em some extra options for the characters.<br /> <br /> Now, I rememeber mages in 1e to be damn strong, and I like that. During the V:TR chronicle the players looked for a way to break blood bonds, and after a long research and quest I pointed them to mages, remembering how awesome they were. Now I would like to ask you if we played spellcasting good in our first game, cause the cabal got pretty buffed up.<br /> <br /> they basically spent their day off casting spells with weekly duration, ritually.<br /> -The obrimos, using Life arcanum, used honing the form to increase the cabal physical traits with a single spell. He over reached a bit, but at Gnosis 2 the paradox didn't really get a lot of dice to roll and he reduced it with mana. He gave the cabal +2 to stamina and strengh, for a week.<br /> -The Acanthus did the same with a rote spell, casting superlative luck and granting the entire cabal +5dices on 5 mundane rolls to spend during the entire week. thanks to his rote he didn't over reach, so no paradox was rolled.<br /> -The mastigos used a rote for augment mind, increasing wits and resolve of the cabal by +2, for an entire month. he contained paradox by mana and a wisdom roll, getting a single resistant bashing damage in the end.<br /> <br /> they all took 3 ritual intervals for this casting, with two yantras in each. next, the acanthus did an instant cast to grant rote actions for 3 times, on a duration of a week, for the entire cabal. he used a rote on this one too, so he paradox only had a couple dices (1 for over reaching a single time, one extra since it was his second cast in the same scene). He spent a couple mana, and paradox only had a chance die, nothing bad happened. He then relinquished the spell using a willpower point<br /> <br /> I really like that right now the cabal really feels like the awakened superhumans they should be. They have high stats pretty much everywhere they need, they have stupid dice bonus and luck, and they still have extra space for more upgrades. did we play everything right? it looks like that cabals would normally always be buffed up weekly/monthly, depending on their power level, doing that in a day off.<br /> <br /> coming from V:TR, they are a bit more squishy (although mage armor helps a lot in this regard), but they have absolute versatility! and this was just passive buffs, I'm pretty sure they can do some pretty awesome stuff in tense situations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25395,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25395-empe999","user":"empe999","date":". 06-24-2020, 05:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25395-empe999","name":"empe999","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T08:09:22-07:00","id":1398603,"title":"","content":"A cabal prepping itself ahead of time for overall preparedness like that at low Gnosis is a bit unusual ime, mostly because you potentially run into spell control problems, but it's not impossible or out of bounds. Sounds fine to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T09:04:51-07:00","id":1398608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1398569-first-mage-chronicle-not-sure-about-power-level?p=1398603#post1398603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A cabal prepping itself ahead of time for overall preparedness like that at low Gnosis is a bit unusual ime, mostly because you potentially run into spell control problems, but it's not impossible or out of bounds. Sounds fine to me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Cool! I like to see the we played the &quot;buffing&quot; without big mistakes. The players all have gnosis 2, so they are each upkeeping a single spell and have one free spell slot. The acanthus is the only one that has been brave enough to relinquish his spell, he hopes that with the weekly duration it won't go to bad. After all it's an acanthus, he likes to push his luck <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> I love the feeling that &quot;mages can do nearly anything&quot;,it's so much different from V:tR. They'll probably face a combat encounter soon enough, and I'm not sure what to expect. They got so many options compared to the &quot;I frenzy and maul them&quot; that often happens in Vampire, but as far as sheer dices are concerned, the +5 dices from the acanthus and the stat buffs seem to make them very strong. The mastigos still has an empty spell slot, he could enhance the fighting skills of the entire cabal if needed. Their only real downside, compared to the vamps, is lethal damage from nearly everything (although most of them will have good mage armor on).<br /> <br /> But I think it should be that way, they are the awakened after all, they literally shape the world when casting <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25395-empe999","name":"empe999","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T08:44:55-07:00","id":1398790,"title":"","content":"I think the answer relates to the kind of game you're running, the way your setting works.<br /> <br /> If the mood of your game is paranoia and the constant threat of unseen danger, then yeah it makes sense.<br /> <br /> If mages in your setting generally rely on the Lex Magica (the rule of law) for protection and generally feel secure, then the cabal is going to look like a gang walking around in bullet proof vests with AR-15s strapped to their backs. It may be legal, but they're going to draw attention and make others nervous.<br /> <br /> You can influence whether your players keep putting this much work into buffing themselves based on how your storyteller characters react to the player characters. A simple &quot;You guys expecting trouble?&quot; and an arched eyebrow can send a message. Some mage gathering places may not allow entrance to mages who seem prepped for a fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","user":"galivet","date":". 06-25-2020, 11:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T23:33:02-07:00","id":1399220,"title":"","content":"That acanthus isn't too far away from simply walking around with a hung spell or two to release as a situation demands..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-28T07:58:21-07:00","id":1399598,"title":"","content":"The Acanthus doesn't even have to have their own spells in the Hung Spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T02:24:12-07:00","id":1400479,"title":"","content":"Wow quite some buffing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Potency shoult be 1 for each of those spells.<br /> Spellcontrol ist another thing. Superlative luck can bring in quite some Paradox.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Gamelines: Requiem, Lost, Awakening, Trinity Continuum: Aeon, some V5.<br /> Likes cheesecake (quark-based)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1305-maekkel","name":"maekkel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-02T09:53:38-07:00","id":1400535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maekkel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1398569-first-mage-chronicle-not-sure-about-power-level?p=1400479#post1400479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow quite some buffing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Potency shoult be 1 for each of those spells.<br /> Spellcontrol ist another thing. Superlative luck can bring in quite some Paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>Potency can be whatever you set it at. They said there was no risk of Paradox on the Superlative Luck, so I don't see how it would bring in any.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}